course: dictionary
lesson: 2829
title: Divination and clues in context
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Divination means trying to find out about the future or hidden things by special or magical means. People might read cards, stars or tea leaves to do it.
explain: «In the Han era Chinese thinkers used magnetic spoons for divination (trying to tell the future).» The brackets are a context clue: they tell you straight away that divination means trying to tell the future.
explain: Divination can also mean a clever guess or insight. Use the swap check: put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. «The spoons were used for trying to tell the future» fits, so your meaning is right.
fact: Divination means trying to find out the future or hidden things by special or magical means.
fact: «Divination» is an uncountable noun, but you can also say «a divination» when you mean one particular guess or prediction.
fact: Many ancient peoples practised divination, such as the oracle at Delphi.
fact: In science, divination is an example of a claim that has no scientific evidence.
fact: Divination can also mean a clever guess or insight.
exercise: «In the Han era Chinese thinkers used magnetic spoons for divination (trying to tell the future).» What does divination mean here? | *Trying to tell the future | Making spoons from magnets | Cooking with iron tools | Sailing across the sea
exercise: Nadia guesses the rain before anyone checks the sky, and her friend says, «That was pure divination!» What does divination suggest here? | A map of the sea | *A clever guess or insight | A kind of cooking | A loud shout
exercise: In a fantasy story, a witch reads the stars to see what will happen next. What is the witch doing? | Painting a map | *Practising divination | Cleaning the castle | Baking bread
test: In science lessons, divination is an example of what? | A kind of cooking | *A claim with no scientific evidence | A proven fact about the stars | A famous scientist
test: Which phrase from the lessons means doing divination? | *practise divination | make a spoon | sail at sea | bake a cake
exam: Which best explains divination? | A loud noise made by the wind | Doing sums quickly in your head | A type of ancient coin | *Trying to find out the future or hidden things by special or magical means
